\section{Calculations}

% A Python cell: it runs when compiling and does not appear in the PDF.
%#python
plot_area = 25.0 * 40.0      # m²
coverage = 0.35              # site coverage ratio
floor_area = plot_area * coverage
%#end

The plot is \py{plot_area}~m$^2$ and, with a site coverage of
\py{round(coverage*100)}~\%, it allows \py{floor_area}~m$^2$ of building.
\pyif{floor_area > 300}{It is a large area.}{It is a small area.}

Change the numbers of the cell and compile again: the text adjusts by itself.
